1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,000
[narrator] Heavens Arena.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,000
The 251-story building

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:09,000
which stands 991-meter tall,

4
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,000
is a mecca for fighters.

5
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,000
When combatants win a fight,
they may advance by one class,

6
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,000
and receive a corresponding reward.

7
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:21,000
After reaching the 100th floor,

8
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,000
they are assigned a private room.

9
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:24,000
And those contestants

10
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:28,000
who are skilled and fortunate enough
to reach the 200th floor

11
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:32,000
earn the right to challenge
the strongest fighters, the Floor Masters,

12
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,000
in an intense battle for survival.

13
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:38,000
This is without a doubt

14
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:41,000
the best stage a warrior could ask for.

15
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:51,000
[theme song playing]

16
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,000
You say that your brother...

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,000
is able to use Nen?

18
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:12,000
I need to understand
what Nen and Ren even mean!

19
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:14,000
And not just halfway.

20
00:02:14,000 --> 00:02:16,000
I need to know it!

21
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:20,000
Well, in that case…

22
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:26,000
NEN X AND X NEN

23
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
[narrator] After Killua fought Zushi,

24
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:32,000
the young practitioner
of Shingen-ryu martial arts,

25
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Zushi mentioned the Four Exercises.

26
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Gon and Killua are about to learn
the secret of those principles

27
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:41,000
from Zushi’s master, Wing.

28
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:45,000
[Wing] Paying attention?

29
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Nen, or flame,
is a power that fires our souls.

30
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
In other words,
it’s the strength of your will.

31
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:54,000
NEN (FLAME)

32
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:56,000
And the Four Exercises

33
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:00,000
is a training regimen
that strengthens your will.

34
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:01,000
“Strengthens your will”

35
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Training?

36
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:04,000
-[pen squeaking on the board]
-[Wing] Correct.

37
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:05,000
TEN (POINT)

38
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
[wing]
Ten: focus the mind on a single point,

39
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
reflect on the self,
and determine the goal.

40
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:12,000
ZETSU (TONGUE)

41
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
Zetsu: to put into words.

42
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:14,000
REN (TEMPER)

43
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:16,000
Ren is to intensify your will.

44
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
HATSU (RELEASE)

45
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Hatsu is to release it into action.

46
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,000
[Gon] Ten. Zetsu. Ren. Hatsu.

47
00:03:24,000 --> 00:03:26,000
The Four Exercises.

48
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,000
See, Zushi tempered his ‘refusal to lose’

49
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:30,000
during his battle with you, Killua.

50
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:37,000
[shuddering breath]

51
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:43,000
[Wing] Now allow me to demonstrate.

52
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Killua?

53
00:03:45,000 --> 00:03:48,000
For this demonstration,
I would like to “kill” you now.

54
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:50,000
Is that all right?

55
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:51,000
Sure. Why not.

56
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,000
But you won’t be able to.

57
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:55,000
Let’s do this in order.

58
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:57,000
First, Ten.

59
00:03:59,000 --> 00:04:01,000
I focus my mind on a single point.

60
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
Zetsu:

61
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Express your desired intent.

62
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Either mentally or verbally.

63
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:14,000
I will kill you.

64
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[quiet grunt]

65
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
That was a taste of Ren.

66
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:01,000
With enough strength and focus,

67
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
the will functions as action or Hatsu.

68
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
With a strong will

69
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
your opponent will back down.

70
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
A more familiar term would be ‘bluffing’.

71
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
Ren hardens that which is soft

72
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
and you suddenly find
that you’ve lost your ability

73
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
to correct an incorrect idea.

74
00:05:21,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Therefore, until your soul
has fully matured,

75
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
avoid using Ren.

76
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:26,000
As it stands now,

77
00:05:26,000 --> 00:05:29,000
you three boys should really focus
on training your souls.

78
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[Killua] Let's go, Gon.

79
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
[Wing]
If you truly wish to learn about Nen,

80
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
set your sights on mastering Ten first.

81
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
If you master Ten,

82
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:47,000
you no longer feel the pressure
of an opponent’s will.

83
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:54,000
[Gon] Thank you very much!

84
00:05:59,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Wait up, Killua!

85
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,000
-[Wing] Zushi.
-Yes, sir?

86
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
[Wing] Let's begin training.

87
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:07,000
Oh... Osu!

88
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:10,000
First off…

89
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
[Gon] He lied?

90
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Yeah.

91
00:06:17,000 --> 00:06:19,000
What he said was true, far as it went

92
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
and his power is the real deal, too.

93
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,000
There are a few things it doesn’t cover.

94
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:25,000
Like?

95
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:27,000
[Killua] Like how tough Zushi is.

96
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
In our fight,

97
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:31,000
he got up every time I knocked him down.

98
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:33,000
That was pretty annoying.

99
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
Which is why I got
a little pushy with him at the end.

100
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,000
[cheering]

101
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:44,000
[panting]

102
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Why, you--!

103
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,000
[gasps]

104
00:06:57,000 --> 00:06:58,000
[gasps]

105
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,000
Oops!

106
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:06,000
[commentator]
Oooh! Zushi sails out of the ring!

107
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:08,000
And straight to the hospital,
by the looks of it!

108
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
That’s gotta hurt!

109
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
[cheering]

110
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,000
[commentator] He’s gotten back up, folks!

111
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Zushi must be invincible!

112
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:22,000
[panting]

113
00:07:23,000 --> 00:07:25,000
[Killua] No way…

114
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:29,000
[commentator] But the referee has awarded
a critical hit and knockdown.

115
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:33,000
Killua wins by TKO, with 11 total points.

116
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:36,000
[cheering]

117
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
It wasn’t his strength of will alone

118
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:40,000
that kept him standing that whole time.

119
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:42,000
There’s gotta be something else
he’s hiding.

120
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
[Wing] What’s the matter, Zushi?

121
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:52,000
Your Ten is aggravated.

122
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Master...

123
00:07:55,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[Wing] Hm?

124
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:00,000
Why did you lie to Gon and Killua
just now?

125
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Lie?

126
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:04,000
Are you referring to my explanation?

127
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,000
[Zushi] Yes!

128
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:10,000
The Four Exercises are Ten, Zetsu,
Ren and Hatsu.

129
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
But they don’t mean what you told them.

130
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Did you decide to lie to them
because they aren’t your students?

131
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
FLAME

132
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
[Wing] I didn't lie.

133
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,000
That ‘Nen’ is an important discipline
in training the mind...

134
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:25,000
[pen squeaking on the board]

135
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:27,000
...for this Nen.

136
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:29,000
NEN (MIND FORCE)

137
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:34,000
However, it’s true that I cannot teach Nen
to someone who is not a student.

138
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
So, I used the other Nen as a hint,

139
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
just to help them along.

140
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
If the Nen I teach
is used in the wrong way,

141
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
it can become a terrible weapon, Zushi.

142
00:08:47,000 --> 00:08:48,000
For example…

143
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:49,000
[paper tearing]

144
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
You could turn a simple piece of paper

145
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:20,000
into quite a harmful blade.

146
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:24,000
Furthermore, you could harden your body
as a defensive measure.

147
00:09:27,000 --> 00:09:30,000
With enough work, anyone can use Nen.

148
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
Which is why

149
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:34,000
you must be very careful
when choosing who to teach it to.

150
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Master…

151
00:09:39,000 --> 00:09:40,000
It’s just...

152
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
that I hadn’t gotten the chance
to read that book yet.

153
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,000
Huh?

154
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:46,000
And that juice…

155
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:47,000
it was mine…

156
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
[Wing mumbles]

157
00:09:49,000 --> 00:09:50,000
[Wing] I’m sorry!

158
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
[cheering]

159
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
[commentator] It’s time
for the biggest match of the day!

160
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Two rookies have advanced
to the 190th floor

161
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:06,000
without losing a single fight!

162
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
Gon and Killua!

163
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Will they be able to clear
today’s match in one shot, too?

164
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:16,000
Okay, everyone!

165
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Get ready to press your wager buttons!

166
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
[Kung Fu guy] [scoffs]
Unfortunately for you,

167
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:27,000
that little push move of yours
won’t work on me.

168
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
That’s because...

169
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:33,000
I’m as slippery as a snake,
and my fangs are just as sharp.

170
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:37,000
Fangs that are just dying
for a taste of your vital points.

171
00:10:40,000 --> 00:10:44,000
[Wrestler] [laughs]
You might sport a vicious chop, kid,

172
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:47,000
but it won’t be enough
to save you from these muscles!

173
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:49,000
And do you wanna know why?

174
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:50,000
[grunts]

175
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:53,000
Because I’m totally ripped, obviously!

176
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
[sighs]

177
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:58,000
And begin!

178
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
[kung fu kiai]

179
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:02,000
[roaring]

180
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
[cheering]

181
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:14,000
That’s a critical hit and knockdown!

182
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
That’s three points! It’s a knock out!

183
00:11:17,000 --> 00:11:19,000
And, winner is Gon!

184
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Critical hit and knockdown!

185
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:25,000
That’s three points!

186
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Knockout!

187
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Killua wins!

188
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:31,000
[cheering]

189
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[commentator] Once again, Gon and Killua

190
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:36,000
have knocked out their opponents
with one attack,

191
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:41,000
meaning both of them have successfully
cleared the 190th floor!

192
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Both competitors advance
to the 200th floor!

193
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:48,000
The 200th floor already?!

194
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
[Wing] Zushi.

195
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,000
Master, Wing!

196
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:56,000
Killua and Gon have already reached
the 200th, have they?

197
00:11:56,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Yes! They’re both amazing fighters!

198
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:01,000
I really need to train m--

199
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:03,000
What the--?

200
00:12:04,000 --> 00:12:05,000
Master?

201
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:16,000
[Wing]
I guess I don’t have a choice.

202
00:12:17,000 --> 00:12:18,000
Enjoy.

203
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:28,000
The 200th floor!

204
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
So, what’s it like?

205
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:30,000
Beats me.

206
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:32,000
Never actually been there.

207
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
But I guess we’re gonna find out.

208
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
[elevator dings]

209
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:48,000
[Gon] Wow!

210
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:51,000
The 200th floor sure is fancy, huh?

211
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,000
[Killua] Where’s reception?

212
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:53,000
RECEPTION DESK

213
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:55,000
[Killua] Maybe this way?

214
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:01,000
We finally made it!

215
00:13:01,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Yeah.

216
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
[both gasp]

217
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
[Gon] What is this?

218
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:23,000
It suddenly feels like we’re in a jungle
swarming with monsters!

219
00:13:24,000 --> 00:13:27,000
But it looks like an ordinary hallway.

220
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Let’s go.

221
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:37,000
We can do this!

222
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:44,000
RECEPTION DESK

223
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
[Gon] It’s not working…

224
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,000
I can’t go on!

225
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:02,000
I don’t want to!

226
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Do you feel that bloodlust?

227
00:14:04,000 --> 00:14:06,000
It’s directed right at us!

228
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:07,000
[straining exhale]

229
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:09,000
[Killua] Okay, that’s enough!

230
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Who’s there?!

231
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:12,000
Show yourself!

232
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
You must be Killua and Gon.

233
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:23,000
The reception desk is this way,

234
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:27,000
so please register
for a 200th match today.

235
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Be advised that your eligibility
for this floor expires at midnight,

236
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
so please don’t delay.

237
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Did that feeling come from her?

238
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:40,000
I can't tell.

239
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:43,000
By the way, on the 200th floor,

240
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
there are currently 173 contestants.

241
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:50,000
And from this floor up,

242
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:53,000
all weapons are allowed in all matches.

243
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:55,000
So, please feel free to use
whatever you have.

244
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Also, as of the 200th floor,

245
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
you will no longer receive prize money.

246
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Now you will be fighting only for honor.

247
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Please keep that in mind,
if you participate.

248
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
[gasps]

249
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Hi-- Hisoka…

250
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
But what are you doing here?

251
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
It isn’t that strange, is it?

252
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
I love to fight

253
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:42,000
and this is a temple devoted to the craft.

254
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
The real question is why are you here?

255
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Just kidding…

256
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
This meeting is no mere coincidence.

257
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I've been waiting for you.

258
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Remember how you ordered your tickets
for the airship over the internet?

259
00:15:59,000 --> 00:16:01,000
With only a little effort on my part,

260
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:05,000
I was able to find out exactly
when you would arrive.

261
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
Well, in any case,

262
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
I knew you would come here eventually.

263
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
And so...

264
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:14,000
as your senior,

265
00:16:14,000 --> 00:16:17,000
I have a little bit of a warning
for the both of you.

266
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:23,000
You’re still not ready
to set foot on this floor.

267
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Not by a long shot.

268
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:30,000
[Gon and Killua grunting]

269
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:35,000
[Hisoka]
When you will be depends on your efforts.

270
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
For now, leave this floor.

271
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,000
It’s far too early.

272
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:41,000
[Killua] Wait, what?!

273
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:43,000
That’s stupid! We just got up here!

274
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:50,000
I won't let you pass.

275
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,000
But it’s not like you could anyway.

276
00:16:54,000 --> 00:16:56,000
[Killua] [grunts] What the hell…?!

277
00:16:57,000 --> 00:16:58,000
[Gon] What is this?!

278
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
[both straining]

279
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,000
[Wing] Don't be reckless!

280
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:16,000
[Gon] Mr. Wing!

281
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:18,000
What he’s saying is true.

282
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
You have no defense against his Nen.

283
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:21,000
Nen?

284
00:17:22,000 --> 00:17:23,000
As it stands,

285
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
you're both naked in a blizzard,

286
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:28,000
both of you wondering why it’s so cold.

287
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:30,000
If you continue to strain your bodies,

288
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:32,000
you may die.

289
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:34,000
So, this is Nen?

290
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:37,000
He can stop us from moving forward
through willpower?

291
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:39,000
You liar!

292
00:17:39,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Yes. I was lying.

293
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,000
Though some of what I said
was technically true.

294
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,000
I will teach you the truth about Nen.

295
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:49,000
So, for the time being,

296
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,000
I suggest we withdraw.

297
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Uh ‘scuse me…

298
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
[receptionist] Oh yes?

299
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:59,000
If we don’t register for a fight today,

300
00:17:59,000 --> 00:18:00,000
how would that affect us?

301
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Well, you would have
to start all over again

302
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:05,000
from the first floor.

303
00:18:05,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Killua, however…

304
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
he’s been here before,

305
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,000
and refused to register.

306
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
So, if he fails to do so again,

307
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
his commitment
will be called into question

308
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
and he will be banned from participating.

309
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
[Killua] Mr. Wing.

310
00:18:24,000 --> 00:18:25,000
If we withdraw,

311
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:28,000
will we be able to make it back here
by midnight?

312
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Hmm...

313
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:39,000
[Wing] That all depends on you.

314
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,000
[Wing] Simply put this is Nen.

315
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
Nen refers to the ability
to control your “aura”

316
00:18:55,000 --> 00:18:58,000
which, as you may know,
is also known as life energy.

317
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,000
NEN (MIND FORCE)

318
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Everyone in the world
has a small amount of life energy.

319
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,000
But in most cases,

320
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:08,000
it simply leaks away.

321
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,000
The ability to build up and contain
this life energy is known as Ten.

322
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:13,000
is called Ten.

323
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
(ENVELOPE)

324
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Using Ten you can make your body tougher

325
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:20,000
and considerably slow
the effects of aging.

326
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
TEN (ENVELOPE)

327
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Then comes Zetsu

328
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:25,000
which shuts off the flow of aura.

329
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:27,000
ZETSU (SUPPRESS)

330
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:30,000
It’s quite effective for concealing
your presence from others

331
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:32,000
and recovering from fatigue.

332
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Which brings us to Ren,

333
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
REN (REFINE)

334
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:38,000
It enables you to produce more aura.

335
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
Can you feel that?

336
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:49,000
Yeah. It’s like pressure…

337
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
But it doesn’t feel weird or creepy.

338
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:55,000
That’s because I have absolutely
no malice.

339
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I must admit I’m impressed.

340
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:01,000
Their senses are amazing.

341
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
Perhaps it’s a product of the environments

342
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,000
in which they were raised.

343
00:20:06,000 --> 00:20:08,000
But their innate gifts are also a factor.

344
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:14,000
Aura is an energy dwelling
within all humans…

345
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:18,000
which makes it very effective
against other humans.

346
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:20,000
For better or for worse.

347
00:20:22,000 --> 00:20:24,000
If you attack a helpless person
with malice,

348
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
you can kill using aura alone.

349
00:20:32,000 --> 00:20:35,000
Only one thing can protect you
from a user of Nen.

350
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:38,000
You must learn to use it yourself

351
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:41,000
and use Ten for defense.

352
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:44,000
Block the other person’s aura
with your own.

353
00:20:47,000 --> 00:20:48,000
Otherwise...

354
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:13,000
Your body will be shattered
beyond all recognition.

355
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:21,000
[narrator] Hisoka blocks the path
leading beyond the 200th floor.

356
00:21:22,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Will Gon and Killua
have begun their studies

357
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:29,000
but will they be able to learn enough
about true Nen to pass Hisoka

358
00:21:29,000 --> 00:21:31,000
and reach the receptionist

359
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:33,000
all before the clock strikes midnight?

360
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
Not yet.

361
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
It’s too soon.

362
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:45,000
[theme song playing]

363
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:53,000
[Gon] Coming up:

364
00:22:53,000 --> 00:22:54,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

365
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
[both] ...Hunterpedia!

366
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

367
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

368
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:03,000
Today, we're introducing Mr. Wing,
Zushi’s master

369
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:05,000
and an expert at Shingen-ryu!

370
00:23:05,000 --> 00:23:07,000
It seems like he’s pretty good with Nen.

371
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:09,000
Oh yeah, but isn’t his shirt untucked?

372
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,000
And he’s got bedhead!

373
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:19,000
Next time: Awakening x And x Potential!

374
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:21,000
[Gon grunting]

375
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Did you feel anything?

376
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
[Killua] Nope. Nothing.
